== casting 1 / FR-037: what this casting touched, and what the tree shows ==

  ADDRESS NOTE. The casting prompt Verification section names
  tests/test_orchestrator_gates.py, which casting 2 carved into
  tests/orchestration/. The package-wide AST and import scans that
  parenthetical is about now live in
  tests/orchestration/test_module_boundaries.py, so that is the file this log
  drives in its place. The claim is unchanged; only its address moved.

  WHAT CHANGED IN THE DEFECT CYCLES. Five defects, all LIVE, all inside this
  castings own two modules.

  fallout D-105 / FR-050 -- THE ROSTER DOOR PUBLISHED A POPULATION NOBODY
  DERIVED. foundry_roster accepted items=[] and wrote the zero-item roster
  file that migrate-archive.py#_migrate_rosters refuses by name to create,
  its docstring stating the ruling for the whole run: a roster FILE holding
  zero items says a stream derived its item list and the list was empty, a
  measurement nobody took. The state WEDGES the stream. Driven at the parent
  commit: foundry_roster(trace, []) returned ok=True with roster_length 0,
  and the real later derivation foundry_roster(trace, [x, y, z]) was then
  refused ROSTER_EXISTS on the strength of it, with every honest items_total
  refused ROSTER_MISMATCH and items_checked=0 refused by the roll-ups own
  positive-count guard. No legal recording was left at all. The refusal now
  sits at publication, beside CONCERN_TEXT_EMPTY on the sibling ledger door.

  fallout D-106 / FR-050 -- AND A DENOMINATOR THAT COUNTED A MEMBER TWICE.
  The roster length is what Foundry-Stream enforces, so a list this door
  accepts is a number no later door is able to question. Driven at the parent
  commit: items=[a, a, b] returned ok=True with items_total 3 for two
  distinct items, so 3 of 3 recorded full coverage of a population one of
  whose members was counted twice -- the double-count _record_stream_rollup
  was rewritten to end, reintroduced one door upstream where the population
  is declared. items=[1, 2] likewise returned ok=True, persisting integers
  where every consumer reads a path or a requirement id. Three named
  refusals now: ROSTER_ITEMS_EMPTY, ROSTER_ITEMS_DUPLICATED and
  ROSTER_ITEM_NOT_NAMED, on the first write and on the revise arm alike.

  fallout D-124 / GI-024 -- THE THIRD TIMESTAMP DERIVATION. GI-024s
  violation column is a second derivation outside foundry_state, and both of
  this castings modules still spelled datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()
  inline while foundry_report._now, the one delegation, documented itself as
  one of only two. Both are call-through bindings to foundry_state.now_iso
  now, which is what _DELIBERATE_REDEFINITIONS says every module binding the
  name is; neither module imports datetime at all any more.

  fallout D-145 and D-146 / FR-039 / ST-004 -- THE CLOSE SUCCEEDED WITH ITS
  GUARD ARTEFACT SILENTLY UNWRITTEN. ST-004s guard column names two
  conditions for the close: reason non-empty, and a handoff record is
  appended. The first was a named refusal; the second was best-effort AND
  silent -- _close_concern discarded _append_close_handoff s outcome and the
  appender swallowed the failure in except (ImportError, OSError): return.
  Driven at the parent commit with handoffs.jsonl made a directory: the close
  returned ok=true with no handoff record anywhere and nothing on the result
  to say so, while the same arrangement on concerns.md returned ok=true WITH
  render_problem naming the failure, one line up in the same function. The
  asymmetry was the defect rather than the decision to let the close proceed:
  the entry is closed inside a committed transaction before the handoff is
  attempted at all. The appender returns a problem string now, in
  render_concerns_markdowns own str-or-None contract, and the close surfaces
  it as handoff_problem beside render_problem.

  WHAT CHANGED IN THE CONCERN CYCLES. Two cross-casting concerns, both filed
  against this castings files by another casting, both closed here.

  fallout FR-009 / AC-005 (casting 7s concern C-080) -- THE LEDGERS OWN DOOR
  COULD NOT BE TOLD ABOUT A DIRECTORY. resolve_target matched a target
  against key_files as exact or a tail on a segment boundary, so a concern
  naming any module beneath casting 2s .../tools/orchestration/ resolved to
  nothing -- the refusal a filer hits at precisely the moment it has found
  something in that package. A second pass now asks coverage, and the
  reading is the leafs by import: concerns.py calls keyfiles.covers_path
  rather than holding a fifth spelling of what a key_files entry is.

  fallout D-167 (casting 2s concern C-083) -- THE HOUSE REFUSAL SHAPE WAS
  TWO BYTE-IDENTICAL BODIES. rosters.py holds the one implementation and
  concerns.py binds it, which is the _now arrangement the boundary guard
  already names as closed. A bare re-export was not available: casting 2s
  own AST pin asserts concerns.py DEFINES the name, and casting 2 has
  finished, so deleting the definition would have left a red tree with
  nobody able to green it.

  NOTHING IS DESELECTED, AND THE SELECTION IS WHOLE. No deselects and no
  qualifications: every rung below runs, and every rung below passes.

  WHAT FR-037 CLAIMS HERE, precisely. This casting touched no file outside its
